# GitHub Auto Push

A lightweight macOS shell automation tool for automatically committing and pushing local project changes to GitHub.

## Features

- Detects local Git changes automatically
- Creates commits with timestamps
- Pushes changes to the current Git branch
- Includes basic `.gitignore` protection
- Simple command-line workflow
- Designed for repeatable GitHub publishing

## Usage

Make the script executable:

```bash
chmod +x scripts/autopush.sh
# Test GitHub Auto Push

This is a test repository created and pushed from a local Mac script.

## What it does

- Initializes a Git repository
- Creates an initial commit
- Creates a GitHub repository
- Pushes local files to GitHub
